<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">O'More</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Uí Mórda, Ó Mórdha</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The O'Mores, Irish Ó Mórdha, were the ruling family of the Loígis in the Irish midlands from the 11th century, taking their name from an ancestor called Mórda. They recovered much of their territory from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-normans">Anglo-Normans</a> in the 14th century and resisted the plantation of Laois under Mary I and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-i">Elizabeth I</a>, notably under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rory-og-omore">Rory Óg O'More</a>. Their lands were confiscated and many of the family were killed or transplanted.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/omore.jpg" alt="O'More" width="320" height="352" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: self-created · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:O%27More.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
